WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.834
You look very suave.

00:00:00.918 --> 00:00:03.212
I feel very under-dressed
at this premiere.

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:04.922
-No, you look good!
-I tried, I tried.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:05.881
Urban chic.

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:07.966
Thank you.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.093
Hi, I'm Gena
with Netflix UK.

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:11.678
I'm here
at the London Film Festival

00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:12.804
to be your eyes and ears

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:15.098
for the premiere
of The Harder They Fall.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.602
Please.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.652
We've got lots of exciting
people here tonight.

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.278
We've got Jeymes Samuel,

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:30.113
who is the writer
and director of the film.

00:00:30.197 --> 00:00:31.323
We've got Idris Elba.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:33.951
I was promised Jay-Z.
I hope I get to see Jay-Z.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.078
We've got Jonathan Majors,
Edi Gathegi.

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.704
We've got tons
of exciting people.

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:41.625
Oh my fucking God!

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.836
Now, Jeymes Samuel,
you're the director, writer,

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:44.962
you're the man
behind it all.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.840
I'm also the composer
of the entire score.

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.341
You've done bits.

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:50.425
You're from London.

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:52.052
You can tell,
just by the way you are,

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:53.262
you're a London guy.

00:00:53.345 --> 00:00:54.721
-Harrow Road.
-Is it?

00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:56.723
-I'm from Southeast.
-I love Southeast.

00:00:56.807 --> 00:00:58.892
Right, right.
I'm from South London, but…

00:00:58.976 --> 00:00:59.893
What must it feel like?

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:01.937
I mean, this is your
directorial debut.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.272
You're here premiering it,

00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:06.608
London Film Festival,
in London, right?

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:09.069
It's on Netflix.
What was that journey like?

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:10.654
You must be so proud
of what you achieved.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:14.074
I'm so proud, really,
of what you've achieved,

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:15.951
what I've achieved,
what everyone's achieved.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:17.077
-This is our movie.
-Yeah.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.787
What was it like
partnering with Jeymes

00:01:18.871 --> 00:01:20.706
and doing the work
with the rest of the cast?

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:21.748
He made it easy

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:24.960
because Jeymes
has energy, enthusiasm.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:26.837
He stays positive every day.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.005
-Yeah.
-I mean…

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.089
And you know,

00:01:29.173 --> 00:01:32.301
he has such an incredible
vision for this movie.

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:36.013
He knew every single frame
of what he wanted.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.222
-Right, yeah.
-You know?

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:40.017
This is our movie, man.
Like, from London…

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.812
From when we're in London,
or America…

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:46.857
Gosh. You all love
each other so much.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:49.610
The inspiration
for the music is just like,

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:50.736
you know,

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:53.197
westerns and that genre,
influenced the world,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.365
because at one point,
it was the only thing on TV,

00:01:55.449 --> 00:01:57.576
like everything
on free access TV.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:59.286
-Yeah.
-So it influenced the world.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:02.456
You'd go to Jamaica and see
people dressed as cowboys.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:05.250
And you know, how that
influenced the culture…

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.461
Sorry. Just waiting for her.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:08.754
Then for us to bring it

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:10.923
all the way back full circle
was just beautiful.

00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:12.591
So, your list
of accolades is long.

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:14.635
It's long. You've been
in all sorts, everywhere.

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:16.512
-I've been about.
-Yeah, you've been about.

00:02:16.595 --> 00:02:18.597
What drew you to this film
in particular?

00:02:19.306 --> 00:02:20.641
Just the uniqueness,
you know?

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:22.184
I mean,
I love westerns, period,

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.019
but I've never seen
a western like this.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:26.772
The way it was written
and he brought it together,

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:29.733
the styling, the impact
he wanted it to make,

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.569
was really, like,
different and unique.

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:35.572
It's a story that
really pushes narrative,

00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:38.367
and breaks genre
and expands genre.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.536
Build muscle by tearing it.
That's how you get strong.

00:02:40.619 --> 00:02:42.704
And so, as the audience,
we all had to do that.

00:02:42.788 --> 00:02:44.164
I know I had to do that,
personally.

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:47.501
-And everybody deserves it.
-Right.

00:02:47.584 --> 00:02:50.420
The culture deserves it.
This festival deserves it.

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:53.924
Those who cried,
and sweat, and bled over it,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:54.925
they deserve it.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.885
And it's here,
so let's roll.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.680
Clearly, you don't know me.

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:01.431
What are you most proud of?

00:03:01.515 --> 00:03:04.101
I mean, that we made it
to the finish line

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.144
and we're here right now,
that is…

00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:09.940
This film just had
so many odds against it,

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:12.484
with shooting in a pandemic.

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:14.820
At one point, it was like,
"Are we coming back?

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:16.655
Are we gonna
finish this film?"

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:19.074
And because everyone
really believed in it

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:21.034
and really wanted
to see it through,

00:03:21.118 --> 00:03:24.288
because it is so unique,
as you pointed out,

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:30.377
to just be here
and celebrate it is beyond.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.671
The favourite part
comes from the sadness

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:34.089
of the pandemic,
to be honest.

00:03:34.173 --> 00:03:37.593
Because we all were
right there, ready to shoot.

00:03:37.676 --> 00:03:38.510
Yeah.

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:41.847
And I caught Covid,
and it stopped.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.265
And so, from that point on,

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:45.475
we became a family
and we bonded.

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:46.768
-You can really tell.
-Yeah.

00:03:46.852 --> 00:03:48.812
And now, you know,
we made the film,

00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:51.690
but we feel really
close to each other.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.942
Shit ain't gonna
end well for you.

00:03:57.362 --> 00:03:58.739
Really?

